1
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,090
Hi, Grandpa.

2
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:26,780
Hi, Robbie.

3
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,120
Can I help?

4
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,210
Yes, indeed.

5
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:33,480
Hand me two eggs from the refrigerator,

6
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:37,870
and I'll make you two fried eggs.

7
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:40,100
How about some bacon?

8
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:43,090
I made enough for an army.

9
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:45,540
You going to the baseball game today?

10
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:49,950
It's a perfect day for it--a little cloudy but nice and warm.

11
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:52,100
Dad and I were planning to go to the game,

12
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,680
but he has to work today,

13
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,540
and my friends don't want to go.

14
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,980
It's not an important game, anyway.

15
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:00,590
Do you have any other plans for the day?

16
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:02,580
I'll work on my computer.

17
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,880
I have a new math program, and I want to learn how to use it.

18
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:07,370
Maybe you can teach me

19
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:09,120
how to work on a computer someday.

20
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:12,870
Anytime. It's really easy, but, like anything,

21
00:01:12,870 --> 00:01:17,230
you need to work at it, Grandpa.

22
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:18,770
This bacon is great.

23
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:21,450
I love crispy bacon.

24
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:23,900
Oh, what are you doing tomorrow?

25
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:26,580
Nothing much.

26
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:31,650
Well, maybe your dad and I could take you fishing with us.

27
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:33,370
I'd like that, but ...

28
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:35,900
But what?

29
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:38,030
But Dad is always so busy.

30
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:43,540
Well, can you come fishing with me tomorrow?

31
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:47,600
Sure, I can.

32
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,490
Robbie says you can't take him to the game today.

33
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:51,990
I really feel bad about it,

34
00:01:51,990 --> 00:01:53,790
but they need me at the hospital today,

35
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:55,390
in the children's ward.

36
00:01:55,390 --> 00:01:57,850
I understand.

37
00:01:57,850 --> 00:02:00,260
Maybe we can spend some time together next weekend.

38
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,540
Definitely.

39
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,630
We should.

40
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:05,880
You and Robbie and me.

41
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,310
Remember our first fishing trip?

42
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:10,230
I sure do....

43
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:13,930
Well, I've got to run, Dad.

44
00:02:13,930 --> 00:02:17,200
See you later.

45
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,640
Going fishing?

46
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:22,330
I'm thinking about it....

47
00:02:22,330 --> 00:02:23,820
So, how's work?

48
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:26,950
Oh, the usual problems.

49
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:29,240
You're working pretty hard these days.

50
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:33,660
I guess I am.

51
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:37,450
When did you last go fishing with Robbie?

52
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:39,780
I remember exactly.

53
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:44,620
It was on his birthday, June second, two years ago.

54
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:48,310
We didn't catch anything.

55
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:50,100
Remember our fishing trips?

56
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:55,630
Yes. I loved them.

57
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:59,600
Remember catching your first fish?

58
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:00,500
How can I forget?

59
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:05,280
I fell out of the boat!

60
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:07,520
We had some good times together.

61
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,430
Yes, we did.

62
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:14,000
Maybe we should do it again.

63
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,080
How about tomorrow?

64
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,590
Don't you have to work?

65
00:03:17,590 --> 00:03:20,380
My paper work will wait.

66
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:23,180
Oh, Robbie will be thrilled.

67
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,170
I am, too, Son.

68
00:03:25,170 --> 00:03:27,070
I want to spend more time with Robbie.

69
00:03:27,070 --> 00:03:29,010
Tomorrow.

70
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:31,400
It'll be like old times for you and me.

71
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,590
And Robbie will love it.

72
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:38,110
Well, what's the weather going to be like?

73
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:45,210
Radio says sunny and mild.

74
00:03:45,210 --> 00:03:49,460
Well, I'll tell Robbie.

75
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:53,300
And thanks, Dad.

76
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:54,510
Don't thank me.

77
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:57,510
I'm just being a grandfather.
